          "english": "Swipe(刷卡) is the operative word: cards are increasingly vulnerable to attacks when you make purchases in a store. In several recent incidents, hackers have been able to obtain massive information of credit-debit-(借记) or prepaid-card numbers using malware, i.e. malicious software, inserted secretly into the retailers' point-of-sale system—the checkout registers. Hackers then sold the data to a second group of criminals operating in shadowy corners of the web. Not long after, the stolen data was showing up on fake cards and being used for online purchases.",
          "chinese": "“刷卡”是关键所在：当你在商店购物时，卡片越来越容易受到攻击。在最近发生的几起事件中，黑客能够利用恶意软件，也就是秘密植入零售商销售点系统（即收银机）的恶意软件，获取大量信用卡、借记卡或预付卡卡号。随后，黑客将这些数据卖给在网络阴暗角落活动的第二伙犯罪分子。没过多久，被盗数据就出现在假卡上，并被用于网上购物。",
